lanes.shape:
The two rider fields exist but are each too narrow, singular, and applied from feats only. Make BOTH arrays (one record often needs two different riders — Fearsome Fangs steps jaws d8->d12, two steps, and claws d6->d8, one), move them onto DefenseGrants so ClassFeature inherits them, and add the missing verbs.

unarmedTraits?: {
  match?: string[];                 // existing: name substring
  fromRecord?: string;              // NEW: match the strike a specific RECORD granted. 'Claw' is the name of
                                    //   Draconic Aspect's attack AND of a nephilim's Bestial Manifestation,
                                    //   so a name match hands Deadly Aspect's deadly d8 to the wrong character.
  add?: string[];
  remove?: string[];                // NEW: 'your fist attacks lose the nonlethal trait'. Every field to date only adds.
  stepDie?: boolean | number;       // NEW: a COUNT, not a flag
  setDie?: string;                  // NEW: the absolute die, which is how these are printed ('increases to 1d12')
  stepDieIfHad?: boolean;           // existing
  critSpec?: boolean;               // NEW: THIS strike gets its group's crit specialization even with no other
                                    //   source. critSpecWeapons can filter by group/trait/base — never by one attack.
}[]

weaponTraits?: {
  match?: { melee?: boolean; groups?: string[]; anyTrait?: string[]; items?: string[];
            categories?: WeaponCategory[];   // NEW: 'simple weapons you wield' (Humble Strikes)
            hands?: 1 | 2;                   // NEW: 'any ONE-HANDED axe weapon you wield'
            excludeTraits?: string[];        // NEW: Integrated Gauntlet excludes two-hand / fatal-aim
            maxBulk?: number;                // NEW: Inconspicuous Appearance's 'if light Bulk, also concealable'
            deityFavored?: true;             // NEW: Deific Weapon
            designated?: 'innovation' | 'weapon-implement' | 'bonded' | 'ikon';  // NEW — see lane 4
          };
  add?: string[]; remove?: string[]; onlyIfMissing?: boolean;
  stepDie?: boolean | number; setDie?: string; damage?: { dice:number; die:DieSize; type:DamageType };
  range?: { set?: number; add?: number };   // NEW: there is no range lane at all today
}[]

Also: RuneDef.damage gains `condition?: string` (giant-killing's 1d6/2d6 applies only against giants — the rune payload is otherwise unconditional and would over-grant on every Strike); ELEMENT_BLAST gains an alternate damage-type list with a player pick (versatile-blasts).

This lane also RETIRES two hardcodes. derive.ts:1866 `fistDieUpgraded` is a literal set — `ownedFeatureIds.has('powerful-fist')` plus heritages warrior-automaton / warrior-jotunborn — which is exactly what martial-artist-dedication needs and cannot have; it becomes three data records using `setDie:'d6'`. And the Deadly Simplicity path (derive.ts:988 hasDeadlySimplicity, :994 deitySimpleFavoredWeaponIds, :1006 deityFavorsUnarmed, applied at :1512) is one feat hardcoded into derive; humble-strikes and deific-weapon turn it into one data-driven pass that Deadly Simplicity itself then uses.

`spellListAdditions` EXISTS (types.ts:814) as `{ spells: string[]; entryId?: string }` and is read at build.ts:2659-2667 into Character.spellListAdditions, consumed by SpellsTab.tsx:246-247 — so the surface is PROVEN. Three things make it too narrow: it is singular (one record cannot do two things), it is declared on Feat only (zero classFeatures can carry it), and it only ever widens the PICKER — there is no way to say 'you actually know this' or 'this becomes a legal font spell'.

Make it an array on DefenseGrants:
  spellListAdditions?: {
    spells?: string[];
    entryId?: string;
    from?: 'deity';                  // NEW: resolve the set from the character (Blessed Blood = your deity's cleric spells)
    pick?: number;                   // NEW: 'up to three of your deity's spells'; picks live in BuildState.featSpellListPicks keyed `<recordId>:<i>`
    as?: 'list' | 'repertoire' | 'font' | 'ritual';   // NEW
  }[]
'list' (default) widens only the prepare/repertoire picker — you must still learn them. 'repertoire' actually grants them into entry.grantedRepertoire, free of the known-spells cap. 'font' appends to entry.font.allowed. 'ritual' adds them to the Rituals section as spells you KNOW.

The font half needs no new machinery: build.ts:1971 already ships `entry2.font = { type:'battle', slots, rank, useClassDc:true, allowed:['bane','bless'] }` for the Battle Harbinger, and :1974 pins the ordinary font to a single `{type: build.divineFont}`. versatile-font = allowed ['heal','harm']; restorative-channel appends cleanse-affliction / clear-mind / sound-body / sure-footing; aura-enhancement appends benediction / malediction.

One extra field for three records that print a FIXED sanctification where only a player-picked holy/unholy choice exists today:
  DefenseGrants.sanctification?: 'holy' | 'unholy'   (ghost-path-epiphany).

Extend the EXISTING SpellSlotBonus (types.ts:376) rather than adding a rival field, then add the trading half.

interface SpellSlotBonus {
  perRank?: number; exceptHighest?: number; byRank?: Record<string, number>; entryId?: string;
  cantrips?: number;        // NEW. The applier filters r > 0, so byRank['0'] is silently DROPPED and nothing
                            //   else can reach the cantrip cap. Cantrip Expansion is one of the most-taken
                            //   feats in the game and currently does nothing at all.
  highestOnly?: boolean;    // NEW. Slots at the character's CURRENT highest castable rank (Gifted Power).
                            //   The rank moves with level, so byRank cannot express it and perRank grants ten.
  repertoireToo?: boolean;  // NEW. Spontaneous entries: widen the repertoire by the same count (Frozen Breadth
                            //   grants both 'spells in your repertoire' AND 'spell slots').
  restriction?: string;     // NEW. Printed limit on what the slot may hold. DISPLAY ONLY.
}

Signatures: BuildState.signatures is `Record<rank, string>` (build.ts:223) — one per rank, so a sorcerer cannot designate a second signature at any rank. Change to `Record<rank, string[]>` (or add `extraSignatures?: string[]`), and add `DefenseGrants.extraSignatures?: { count: number; maxRank?: number }` (signature-spell-expansion: 2 at base rank <= 3) plus `allSignatures?: true` (ultimate-polymath) — the engine already produces all-repertoire signatures for the summoner via the `unlimited-signature-spells` feature check at build.ts:1766-1771 and :1788, so that is the exact hook.

Slot TRADING is a distinct, play-state shape: the trade is re-made every morning, so it is PlayState, not BuildState.
  PlayState.slotTrades?: { entryId: string; spend: Record<number, number>; gain: Record<number, number> }
spell-blending: spend two slots of one rank, gain one bonus slot up to two ranks higher (or trade one slot for two extra cantrips). spell-combination: convert one prepared slot of every rank except 1st and 2nd into a slot holding TWO spells (needs a per-slot flag, `combinationSlots?: number[]`). master-summoner: designate one slot to become TWO summoning slots of the same rank. Each is validated against its own printed table.

`advancedAlchemy` (types.ts:775) is the proof this shape works and the proof it was built too narrowly: `{ items: number; addInt?: boolean; atLevel?: { level, items } }` on Feat -> `Character.advancedAlchemy { max, source }` (types.ts:2325), with a Rest-sheet panel. It is alchemist-only, feat-keyed, and hardcoded to alchemical items. Generalise it:

  dailyTemporaryItems?: {
    id: string;                       // a stable key, so two sources don't collide in play state
    label: string;                    // 'Scroll cache', 'Herbal forager'
    count: number | string;           // a formula: scroll-adept is 2 / 3 at master / 4 at legendary spell DC
    countByProficiency?: { key: ProficiencyKey | 'spell-dc'; ranks: Partial<Record<ProficiencyRank, number>> };
    filter: {                         // WHICH items may be chosen — this is the piece that does not exist
      itemType?: 'consumable' | 'weapon' | 'armor';
      traits?: string[];              // ['healing'] for herbal-forager; ['alchemical'] for the alchemist
      categories?: string[];          // 'scroll', 'potion', 'elixir'
      maxLevel?: string;              // '@actor.level' or a literal
      spellRank?: number | { base: number; atLevel?: { level: number; rank: number } };  // scroll caches
      fromKnownFormulas?: true;       // herbal-forager: 'chosen from formulas you know'
      fromSpellbook?: true;           // scroll-adept
    };
  }[]

The answers live in PlayState (they are re-picked every morning, exactly like advancedAlchemy's), and the chosen items appear in inventory flagged temporary so a rest clears and re-prompts them.

Data: basic-scroll-cache {count:1, filter:{categories:['scroll'], spellRank:1}}; expert-scroll-cache {count:1, spellRank:{base:4}}; master-scroll-cache and grand-scroll-esoterica {count:1, spellRank:{base:6, atLevel:{level:20, rank:7}}}; scroll-adept {countByProficiency:{key:'spell-dc', ranks:{expert:2, master:3, legendary:4}}, filter:{categories:['scroll'], fromSpellbook:true}}; herbal-forager {count:1, filter:{traits:['healing'], categories:['alchemical'], fromKnownFormulas:true}}; horn-of-plenty {count:'1 at 1st, 2 at 8th, 3 at 16th', filter:{categories:['elixir','potion'], maxLevel:'@actor.level'}}.

Four records whose entire content is 'add these to the menu that other record already gives you', and no field lets one record reach into another's `choice.options`. The app has the menus: blessed-armament is a classFeature with a `choice` flagged blessedRune and a fixed five-option array; Harbinger's Armament ships a daily `choice` flagged harbingerRune with five options; the domain picker (choice kind 'domains' in Builder.tsx) enumerates strictly content.deities[deityId].domains; ELEMENT_BLAST hardcodes one damage type per element (derive.ts ~1537).

  choiceOptionAdditions?: {
    target: string;                     // the record id whose choice is being widened
    flag?: string;                      // which choice, when the target has more than one
    add?: { value: string; label: string; description?: string }[];
    replace?: boolean;                  // splinter-faith REPLACES the deity's domain list rather than adding
    fromSanctification?: boolean;       // radiant-armament adds Holy OR Unholy depending on yours
  }[]

Data: radiant-armament {target:'blessed-armament', add:[astral, brilliant], fromSanctification:true}; greater-armament {target:'harbingers-armament', add:[brilliant, corrosive, flaming, frost, holy, shock, thundering, unholy]}; splinter-faith {target:'<deity domains>', replace:true, pick:4}; versatile-blasts adds the alternate damage types per element (air/fire -> cold, earth/wood -> poison, metal -> electricity, water -> acid) to the blast damage-type picker that lane 3 introduces.

Verified in derive.ts deriveSpeeds (~1975-2000): every non-land speed source resolves with `speeds[key] = Math.max(speeds[key] ?? 0, v)`. That is deliberate (two sources granting a fly Speed should not stack) but it makes '+5 feet to any fly Speed you already have' literally inexpressible — a SpeedGrants entry of 5 would be swallowed by the max. And the armour Speed penalty is subtracted unconditionally at derive.ts:1926 with no check for any feat.
  speedAdjust?: {
    key: keyof Speeds | 'all' | 'non-land';
    add?: number;                     // applied AFTER the max() pass, only to a speed that is already > 0
    ignoreArmorPenalty?: boolean;     // Unburdened Iron's first clause
    reducePenalty?: number;           // its second: 'reduce any other Speed penalty by 5 feet'
  }[]
Data: winged-warrior-dedication {key:'fly', add:5}; unburdened-iron {key:'all', ignoreArmorPenalty:true, reducePenalty:5}.

RuneDef (types.ts:1751-1763) carries id/name/slot/kind/value/level/price/damage. `damage` is the ONLY payload and it is weapon-side, so an armour property rune can never do anything mechanical. Verified: core.runes.adamantine-echo = {slot:'armor', kind:'property', level:5} and core.runes.assisting = {slot:'armor', kind:'property', level:5} — both are bare registrations.
  RuneDef.actsAs?: { kind: 'potency' | 'striking' | 'resilient' | 'reinforcing'; value: number };
     // adamantine-echo 'functions as a +1 armor potency rune' — it cannot simply BE kind:'potency', because
     // then it would occupy the potency slot instead of a property slot.
  RuneDef.passiveEffects?: ItemPassiveEffects;   // reuse the item shape wholesale rather than inventing a rune one
     // assisting sets Bulk thresholds of 6 + Str (encumbered) and 11 + Str (max), i.e. +1 to both.
Data: adamantine-echo {actsAs:{kind:'potency', value:1}}; assisting {passiveEffects:{bulkLimitBonus:1}}.

Mutagens and elixirs ship as item-driven consumable MODES (core.modes item-* entries, 211 of them from the consumable-modes ruling). ModeDef carries `duration?: string` — a PRINTED string, because the app has no clock — and `modifiers: ModeModifier[]`, where a mutagen's drawback is a genuine negative modifier (item-bendy-arm-mutagen-lesser carries -1 Athletics). Neither can be touched by anything.
  modeAdjust?: {
    match: { traits?: string[]; ids?: string[]; minDuration?: string };
    doubleDuration?: boolean;        // extend-elixir
    suppressNegativeModifiers?: boolean;   // perfect-mutagen: drawbacks of mutagens YOU crafted
  }[]
Data: extend-elixir {match:{traits:['elixir','infused'], minDuration:'1 minute'}, doubleDuration:true}; perfect-mutagen {match:{traits:['mutagen']}, suppressNegativeModifiers:true}.
